# =============================================================================
# File: .env.secret.example
# Version: 2
# Path: .env.secret   (copy this template to `.env.secret`, then fill values)
# Description: TEMPLATE for the Tier-2 secret env file of the LOCAL
#              docker-compose dev stack (loaded LAST by `e2e_stack.sh dev`,
#              `required: false`). Copy to `.env.secret` (git-ignored, NEVER
#              committed) and fill REAL values. CLAUDE.md §4.6.
#
#              Only the genuinely-secret C8 credentials live here ; the rest
#              of the dev stack's config (Arango / MinIO / per-component)
#              comes from `ay_platform_core/tests/.env.test` defaults.
#
#              The values below are FORMAT EXAMPLES (`changeme-…`) — they show
#              the expected shape/length. REPLACE both before any real use.
#              (K8s deployment uses infra/k8s/overlays/dev/.env.secret instead.)
# =============================================================================

# Shared C8 gateway credential — presented by C3/C4/sub-agents as the Bearer
# AND enforced by the LiteLLM proxy as its master_key. Any strong shared
# secret; the `sk-aywizz-…` shape is a convention, not a requirement.
C8_GATEWAY_API_KEY=sk-aywizz-changeme-0123456789abcdef0123

# Master key that ENCRYPTS the LLM provider API keys stored in the in-app
# registry (AES-256-GCM). Provider-independent (D-011): NO provider key in env
# — you register a provider + its key in the HMI (/admin/llm-*) and C8 stores it
# encrypted with this master key + injects it per call.
#   • Format: url-safe base64 of 32 bytes (44 chars). Generate one with:
#       python -c "import os,base64; print(base64.urlsafe_b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())"
#   • REQUIRED to store provider keys. Absent → creating a provider works but
#     saving its key is refused (503) and the HMI shows the key as "not set".
AY_SECRET_MASTER_KEY=YXl3aXp6LUVYQU1QTEUtbWFzdGVyLWtleS0zMmJ5dGU=
